<quiz><question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Analyzing Probability of Stereo Ownership Given Car Ownership in College Students</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>In a sample of \({@total_sudents@}\) college students, \({@car@}\) said they own a car, \({@stereo@}\) said they own a stereo, and \({@car_and_stereo@}\) said they own both a car and a stereo.</p>
<p> What is the probability of a student's having a stereo given the student has a car?</p>
<em>Note: Give your answer in exact form or correct to \(2\) decimal places where necessary.</em>
<p>\(\quad P(\text{Stereo} | \text{Car}) = \) [[input:ans1]][[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>To find the probability of a student having a stereo given that they have a car, we can use the formula for conditional probability:</p>

<p>\(\displaystyle  P(\text{Stereo} | \text{Car}) = \frac{P(\text{Stereo} \text{ and } \text{Car})}{P(\text{Car})} \)</p>

<p>Given:
<ul>
<li>Total number of students (n)\( = {@total_sudents@}\)</li>
<li>Number of students who own a car (Car) \(= {@car@}\)</li>
<li>Number of students who own a stereo (Stereo) \(= {@stereo@}\)</li>
<li>Number of students who own both a car and a stereo (Car and Stereo) \(= {@car_and_stereo@}\)</li>
</ul></p>

<p>We can plug these values into the formula:</p>

<p>\(\displaystyle  P(\text{Stereo} | \text{Car}) =  \frac{{@car_and_stereo@}}{{@total_sudents@}} \div \frac{{@car@}}{{@total_sudents@}}= \frac{{@car_and_stereo@}}{{@car@}} ={@ta@} \)</p>

<p>So, the probability of a student having a stereo given that they have a car is \( \displaystyle {@ta@}\) or approximately {@decimalplaces(ta,2)@}.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
